HymnData.Notes:
First two lines mp, crescento third line to mf;
                fourth and fifth lines mp, sixth line mf; "exalted" is
                piano, except in third verse it is forte

**DELETED VS. 3**
Sing, choirs of angels,
Sing in exultation;
O sing, all ye citizens of heav'n above!
Glory to God, all
Glory in the highest;

Tune data: 
MUNICH, Hassen's Neuvermehrtes Gesangbuch, 1693, Har. Felix Mendelssohn, 1847, E-flat in 4/4 with E-flat;
AURELIA, Samuel S. Wesley, 1864, E-flat in 4/4 with G.

CH lists the following as alternate tunes: AIREDALE, Charles V. Stanford; 
BLAENWERN, William P. Rowlands, 1905; HYFRYDOL, Rowland H. Prichard, 1830;
LOVE DIVINE (Stainer), John Stainer, 1889; MORIAH, Welsh hymn tune

Alt tunes: 
BETHANY (SMART), Henry T. Smart, 1857, F in 4/4 with A;
IN BABILONE, Traditional Dutch melody, 18th century/c1710, arranged Julius Rontgen, 1906, G in 4/4 with G
